Title: 
Wireless Basics – Survey Your Own Wi-Fi World 

Aim: 
To analyze nearby Wi-Fi networks and compare their signal strength, 
channels, and Wi-Fi standards.

Observation:
I scanned five nearby Wi-Fi networks using a Wi-Fi Analyzer app. I observed that signal
strength was different for each network.Networks with stronger signals provided better
connectivity.Some networks used the same channel, which may lead to interference and 
reduced performance. Wi-Fi 6 (802.11ax), if available, is more efficient in crowded places
because it supports multiple users with better speed and lower latency. 

Result: The nearby Wi-Fi networks were successfully analyzed and compared.
